    "text": "The instantaneous voltages at three terminals marked <math><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> and <math><mi>Z</mi></math> are given by<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mi>&#160;</mi></math> and<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></math><br />An ideal voltmeter is configured to read rms value of the potential difference between its terminals. It is connected between points <math><mi>X</mi></math> and <math><mi>Y</mi></math> and then between <math><mi>Y</mi></math> and <math><mi>Z</mi></math> . The reading(s) of the voltmeter will be",
